    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipTier` derived field on the owner response.\n\nThe endpoints serve a generated `OwnerDto` (from `openapi.yml`) via `OwnerMapper`, which already computes similar derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`) through mapping expressions. I followed that same pattern rather than adding ad-hoc logic in the responder functions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` property to the `Owner` schema as a `SILVER`/`BRONZE` enum, so the generator produces `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", \u2026)` and a small single-purpose `membershipTier(Owner)` default method: returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE` (null-safe on both fields).\n\nThe rule is derived purely from the owner's own stored fields, consistent with the neighboring `membershipNumber` derivation, so no responder or pipeline changes were needed. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass.",
